      "message": "I\u0027m responding to https://github.com/google/blueprint/pull/176#pullrequestreview-70041215 here since the usage of the dependencies seems to be what it\u0027s talking about.\n\nI was thinking that it would be nice if soong_javac_wrapper were to somehow directly declare the information about what callers will need to depend on in order for the outputs of soong_javac_wrapper to be correct (rather than for every caller to independently redeclare that it\u0027s the same as javac). Perhaps if soong_javac_wrapper ever produces different output than javac, then maybe we\u0027d have soong_javac_wrapper also provide a timestamp file that gets rebuilt whenever the behavior of soong_javac_wrapper changes in a way that we care about.\n\nI suppose that would make it easy to test a change to soong_javac_wrapper against all java files, because a developer could just delete the timestamp file.\n\nWe could for the moment expose a variable called perhaps \"${config.JavacWrapperCorrectnessDeps}\", set it equal to \"${config.JavacCmd}\" with a comment, and replace the existing dependencies from the latter to the former.\n\nThe part about saving stdout wouldn\u0027t be addressed by that though.",
